cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A Calibrated Approach to Integrating Biochemical Evidence for Metabolic Reaction Prioritization in Genome-Scale Metabolic Models"
abstract: >-
  GEM1 integrates genome-scale metabolic modeling (GSMM) with probabilistic
  flux uncertainty estimation, cross-reconstruction-algorithm consensus, and
  a hierarchical, empirically-calibrated confidence score into a single
  reaction-level prioritization metric. Demonstrated using NAFLD/MASLD as a
  first validation case study across three independent transcriptomic
  cohorts, with a full independent arithmetic and provenance audit
  documenting the architecture's reproducibility, its structural
  limitations under strict cross-algorithm consensus gating, and the
  empirical instability of its calibrated weighting at small sample sizes.
